## 1. Architecture

```text
Oracle Database
    ↓
GoldenGate Extract
    ↓
GoldenGate Trail
    ↓
GoldenGate Replicat
    ↓
Hourly Parquet partitions in private S3
    ↓
Spark ingestion
    ↓
Bronze Iceberg CDC tables
    ↓
Current-state, SCD2 and bitemporal curated tables
```

The raw S3 layer is append-only and stores inserts, updates, deletes and truncates as CDC events.

GoldenGate uses three internal steps when producing Parquet in S3:

1. File Writer generates local files.
2. Parquet Event Handler converts the files to Parquet.
3. S3 Event Handler uploads the Parquet files.

The Parquet Event Handler requires Avro OCF as its internal input. Avro is therefore a temporary GoldenGate implementation detail and is not exposed as a data-lake storage layer.

