## 3. Raw S3 layout and hourly partitioning

```text
s3://<raw-bucket>/
  oracle-cdc/
    dptf_source_system=oracle_trade/
      dptf_source_database=trading_prod/
        dptf_source_schema=TRADE/
          dptf_source_table=EXECUTIONS/
            dptf_ingest_date=2026-07-24/
              dptf_ingest_hour=12/
                *.parquet
```

GoldenGate requires File Writer partitioning to first separate data by table before additional partition levels are applied.

The resolved File Writer partition path is propagated to the Parquet and S3 Event Handlers.

The partition fields are:

| Field                  | Description                                                       |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dptf_source_system`   | Stable logical source-system identifier, such as `oracle_trade`.  |
| `dptf_source_database` | Stable Oracle database or PDB identifier, such as `trading_prod`. |
| `dptf_source_schema`   | Oracle schema containing the source table.                        |
| `dptf_source_table`    | Oracle source-table name.                                         |
| `dptf_ingest_date`     | UTC date when GoldenGate processed the event.                     |
| `dptf_ingest_hour`     | UTC hour when GoldenGate processed the event, from `00` to `23`.  |

The hourly partition is based on GoldenGate processing time, not Oracle business time or Oracle commit time.

The original source-operation timestamp remains stored inside every CDC event as:

```text
dptf_source_operation_ts
```

Hourly partitioning does not mean one file per hour. GoldenGate can roll multiple files inside the same hourly partition.

Recommended starting values:

```text
Partition interval:         1 hour
File-roll interval:         10 minutes
Inactivity roll interval:   2 minutes
Maximum staging file size:  256 MB
Parquet compression:        Snappy
Partition timezone:         UTC
```

`maxFileSize`, `fileRollInterval` and `inactivityRollInterval` are independent roll conditions. A file is rolled when an applicable condition is reached.

