## 4. CDC event model

Use GoldenGate operation-oriented formatting:

```properties
gg.handler.filewriter.mode=op
gg.handler.filewriter.format=avro_op_ocf
```

Oracle describes `avro_op` as the verbose operation-oriented format. The OCF variant is required when the output is subsequently converted by the Parquet Event Handler.

The conceptual CDC event contains:

```text
dptf_source_system
dptf_source_database
dptf_source_schema
dptf_source_table
dptf_source_object

dptf_operation_type
dptf_source_operation_ts
dptf_ingestion_ts

dptf_source_csn
dptf_source_transaction_id
dptf_transaction_operation_seq
dptf_trail_position

dptf_primary_keys
dptf_schema_changed
dptf_replicat_group

before image
after image
```

The operation images are:

| Operation |        Before image |    After image |
| --------- | ------------------: | -------------: |
| Insert    |      Not applicable | New row values |
| Update    | Previous row values | New row values |
| Delete    |  Deleted row values | Not applicable |
| Truncate  |      Not applicable | Not applicable |

Oracle’s operation-format examples show updates with `before.*` and `after.*` values and deletes with the before image.

For a primary-key update, use:

```properties
gg.handler.filewriter.format.pkUpdateHandling=delete-insert
```

This represents the change as:

```text
DELETE old primary key
INSERT new primary key
```

