## 5. Raw CDC technical metadata

The `dptf_` prefix identifies data-platform technical fields and prevents confusion with source columns that may have technical-sounding business names.

### 5.1 Metadata configuration

```properties
gg.handler.filewriter.format.metaColumnsTemplate=\
${static[dptf_source_system].oracle_trade},\
${static[dptf_source_database].trading_prod},\
${schema[dptf_source_schema]},\
${table[dptf_source_table]},\
${objectname[dptf_source_object]},\
${optype[dptf_operation_type]},\
${timestamp[dptf_source_operation_ts]},\
${currenttimestampiso8601[dptf_ingestion_ts]},\
${csn[dptf_source_csn]},\
${xid[dptf_source_transaction_id]},\
${opseqno[dptf_transaction_operation_seq]},\
${position[dptf_trail_position]},\
${primarykeysmap[dptf_primary_keys]},\
${metadatachanged[dptf_schema_changed]},\
${groupname[dptf_replicat_group]}
```

From GoldenGate 21.1 onward, metacolumn output must be explicitly configured through `format.metaColumnsTemplate`. The field name inside brackets defines the output name, allowing the use of the `dptf_` prefix.

### 5.2 Source-identification fields

| Field                  | Type   | Description                                                                      |
| ---------------------- | ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dptf_source_system`   | String | Platform-defined identifier for the originating system. Example: `oracle_trade`. |
| `dptf_source_database` | String | Platform-defined Oracle database or PDB identifier. Example: `trading_prod`.     |
| `dptf_source_schema`   | String | Oracle source schema. Generated from `${schema}`.                                |
| `dptf_source_table`    | String | Oracle source table. Generated from `${table}`.                                  |
| `dptf_source_object`   | String | Fully qualified source-object name. Generated from `${objectname}`.              |

Oracle defines `${schema}`, `${table}` and `${objectname}` as template/metacolumn keywords.

### 5.3 Operation and ordering fields

| Field                            | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                                          |
| -------------------------------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dptf_operation_type`            | String    | Source operation. Standard values are `I`, `U`, `D` and `T`.                                                                                                         |
| `dptf_source_operation_ts`       | Timestamp | Timestamp carried in the trail record. All operations in the same unbatched transaction normally share this timestamp. It remains stable when the trail is replayed. |
| `dptf_ingestion_ts`              | Timestamp | Time the GoldenGate formatter processed the operation. This may change when a trail record is replayed.                                                              |
| `dptf_source_csn`                | String    | Source Commit Sequence Number representing the source commit-ordering point.                                                                                         |
| `dptf_source_transaction_id`     | String    | Source Oracle transaction identifier.                                                                                                                                |
| `dptf_transaction_operation_seq` | Long      | Sequence number of the operation within its source transaction.                                                                                                      |
| `dptf_trail_position`            | String    | GoldenGate trail location. Oracle defines this as a 20-character value containing the trail sequence number and RBA.                                                 |
| `dptf_primary_keys`              | Map       | Map whose keys are primary-key column names and whose values are their string representations.                                                                       |
| `dptf_schema_changed`            | Boolean   | `true` on the first operation following a source-table metadata change.                                                                                              |
| `dptf_replicat_group`            | String    | Name of the Replicat process that produced the event.                                                                                                                |

Oracle directly defines:

* `${csn}` as the Source Commit Sequence Number;
* `${xid}` as the source transaction ID;
* `${opseqno}` as the record sequence within the transaction;
* `${position}` as the source trail position;
* `${primarykeysmap}` as the map of primary-key names and values;
* `${metadatachanged}` as the first-operation-after-schema-change indicator;
* `${groupname}` as the Replicat group name.

### 5.4 Before, after and missing values

GoldenGate operation formatting exposes values from before and after the operation.

GoldenGate can also emit:

```text
<column>_isMissing
```

when configured with:

```properties
gg.handler.filewriter.format.includeIsMissingFields=true
```

This distinguishes an explicit Oracle `NULL` from a column absent from the trail image.

```text
PRICE = NULL
PRICE_isMissing = false
```

means that the source value was explicitly null.

```text
PRICE = NULL
PRICE_isMissing = true
```

means that the column was not present in the captured row image.

The property is optional and defaults to `false`.

### 5.5 Spark-derived fields

| Field                    | Type      | Description                                                   |
| ------------------------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dptf_event_id`          | String    | Deterministic event identifier used for replay deduplication. |
| `dptf_processing_run_id` | String    | Identifier of the Spark run that processed the event.         |
| `dptf_processed_at`      | Timestamp | UTC timestamp when Spark successfully processed the event.    |

Recommended event identifier:

```text
SHA-256(
    dptf_source_system
    + dptf_source_database
    + dptf_source_object
    + dptf_trail_position
    + dptf_transaction_operation_seq
    + dptf_operation_type
)
```

`dptf_ingestion_ts` is not included because GoldenGate’s current formatter timestamp can change when a trail record is replayed. The trail operation timestamp and trail position are stable for the original trail record.

