## 6. GoldenGate configuration

### 6.1 Source supplemental logging

The final supplemental-logging settings must be agreed with the Oracle DBA and tested for redo-volume impact.

Example:

```text
DBLOGIN USERIDALIAS <source-alias>

ADD TRANDATA TRADE.EXECUTIONS ALLCOLS
ADD TRANDATA TRADE.ORDERS ALLCOLS
ADD TRANDATA TRADE.TRADES ALLCOLS
```

Use full supplemental column logging only where the CDC event contract requires complete before and after images.

**Oracle verification**

* [Oracle transaction-log requirements](https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/goldengate/core/26/coredoc/prepare-transaction-logs-settings-and-requirements-ogg-oracle.html)
* [LOGALLSUPCOLS](https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/goldengate/core/26/reference/logallsupcols.html)

### 6.2 Extract configuration

```text
EXTRACT EXTTRADE

USERIDALIAS <source-alias>
EXTTRAIL ./dirdat/rt

LOGALLSUPCOLS
UPDATERECORDFORMAT FULL
TRANLOGOPTIONS TRACKSCHEMACHANGES

TABLE TRADE.EXECUTIONS;
TABLE TRADE.ORDERS;
TABLE TRADE.TRADES;
TABLE TRADE.FILLS;
TABLE TRADE.POSITIONS;
TABLE TRADE.SETTLEMENTS;
```

`UPDATERECORDFORMAT FULL` controls whether update before and after images are stored together in one trail record.

`TRACKSCHEMACHANGES` enables source table-level schema changes to be tracked and updates the trail metadata as appropriate. Oracle states that this option is enabled by default from GoldenGate 23.7 onward, but it may still be stated explicitly for clarity.

**Oracle verification**

* [UPDATERECORDFORMAT](https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/goldengate/core/26/reference/updaterecordformat.html)
