## 7. Central ETL metadata table

The platform maintains one row per ETL pipeline:

```sql
CREATE TABLE platform_control.dptf_pipeline_metadata (
    dptf_pipeline_id                       STRING NOT NULL,
    dptf_pipeline_name                     STRING,

    dptf_last_run_id                       STRING,
    dptf_last_run_status                   STRING,
    dptf_last_run_time                     TIMESTAMP,

    dptf_last_processed_partition_time     TIMESTAMP,
    dptf_partition_format                  STRING NOT NULL,
    dptf_partition_timezone                STRING NOT NULL,

    dptf_source_ids                        ARRAY<STRING>,
    dptf_target_ids                        ARRAY<STRING>,

    dptf_created_at                        TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,
    dptf_updated_at                        TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
)
USING iceberg;
```

Logical primary key:

```text
dptf_pipeline_id
```

This table is a data-platform design, not an Oracle GoldenGate system table. Oracle GoldenGate does not prescribe this ETL metadata schema.

