## 8. ETL metadata field definitions

| Field                                | Description                                                                                                                       |
| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dptf_pipeline_id`                   | Stable unique identifier for the ETL pipeline. Example: `oracle_trade_executions_raw_to_bronze`.                                  |
| `dptf_pipeline_name`                 | Human-readable name used in monitoring and reporting.                                                                             |
| `dptf_last_run_id`                   | Identifier of the latest pipeline execution attempt. It may logically reference a separate run-statistics table.                  |
| `dptf_last_run_status`               | Status of the latest execution. Recommended values: `RUNNING`, `SUCCESS`, `FAILED`, `CANCELLED` and `SKIPPED`.                    |
| `dptf_last_run_time`                 | Actual UTC start time of the latest pipeline execution. It is not the data watermark.                                             |
| `dptf_last_processed_partition_time` | Start timestamp of the latest successfully processed partition.                                                                   |
| `dptf_partition_format`              | Partition granularity used to calculate the next partition. Recommended values: `HOURLY`, `DAILY`, `WEEKLY`, `MONTHLY` or `NONE`. |
| `dptf_partition_timezone`            | Timezone used to interpret partition boundaries. Recommended value: `UTC`.                                                        |
| `dptf_source_ids`                    | Stable logical identifiers for datasets read by the pipeline.                                                                     |
| `dptf_target_ids`                    | Stable logical identifiers for datasets written by the pipeline.                                                                  |
| `dptf_created_at`                    | UTC timestamp when the metadata row was inserted. Set automatically and never changed.                                            |
| `dptf_updated_at`                    | UTC timestamp when the metadata row was most recently changed. Set automatically on updates.                                      |

