## 10. Schema evolution

GoldenGate tracks table metadata versions in the trail when schema tracking is enabled.

When metadata changes while File Writer is active, GoldenGate rolls the current file so subsequent output can use the updated table metadata.

The expected Spark handling is:

```text
Nullable column addition:
    Extend the Bronze schema.

Compatible numeric or timestamp widening:
    Cast to the approved Bronze type.

Column rename:
    Apply an explicit mapping.

Column drop:
    Apply a controlled schema deployment.

Incompatible type change:
    Stop or quarantine processing until an explicit mapping is approved.
```

`dptf_schema_changed=true` identifies the first event after the source-table metadata definition changed.

It does not describe which column changed or whether the change is compatible.

Because multiple Parquet files can have different schemas, Spark must normalize the files into the approved Bronze Iceberg schema.

